  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Elevated Technologies Services has $309M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Elevated Technologies Services won 192 awards so far, with an average award size of $1.6M, and obligations are up 352.9% year over year. Elevated Technologies Services saw most FY2026 buying from the Department of Veterans Affairs, which obligated $276M, followed by the General Services Administration with $28M and the Department of Defense with $4M. Elevated Technologies Services works primarily in Other Building Equipment Contractors with $284M in obligations and in Facilities Support Services with $21.3M. Fiscal-year obligations rose to $309M in FY26 after $68.3M in FY25 and $51.1M in FY24, showing a concentrated increase this fiscal year to date. Elevated Technologies Services has additional, much smaller obligations from the Department of Commerce, Department of Agriculture, Department of Justice, Department of the Interior, and Department of Homeland Security. The current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main federal buyers of Elevated Technologies Services?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $276M in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $28M and the Department of Defense obligated $4M. Other buyers include the Department of Commerce ($660K), Department of Agriculture ($172K), Department of Justice ($55.6K), Department of the Interior ($35.5K), and Department of Homeland Security ($5.6K)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and contract types drive Elevated Technologies Services revenue?",
        "body": "Other Building Equipment Contractors is the largest market, with $284M in obligations for FY2026 to date. Facilities Support Services contributed $21.3M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction contributed $3.2M. Smaller repair and specialty categories account for the remaining obligations, including amounts as low as $598K, $12.2K, and $8.2K."
      }
    ]
  },
